<refentry xmlns="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook" version="5.2" id="process_extractleds">

	<refmeta>
		<refentrytitle>process_extractleds</refentrytitle>
		<manvolnum>1</manvolnum>
	</refmeta>

	<refnamediv>
		<refname>process_extractleds</refname><refpurpose>extract LEDs from a video file.</refpurpose>
	</refnamediv>

	<refsynopsisdiv>
		<cmdsynopsis>
		<command>process_extractleds</command>
		<arg><option>-t</option> <replaceable>threshold</replaceable></arg>
		<arg><option>-minsize</option> <replaceable>n</replaceable></arg>
		<arg><option>-maxsize</option> <replaceable>n</replaceable></arg>
		<arg><option>-colors</option> <replaceable>N</replaceable></arg>
		<arg><option>-color</option></arg>
		<arg><option>-smooth</option> <replaceable>alpha</replaceable></arg>
		<arg><option>-n</option></arg>
		<arg><option>-i</option></arg>
		<arg><option>-i2</option></arg>
		<arg><option>-hide</option></arg>
		<arg choice="plain">
			<replaceable>file</replaceable>
		</arg>
		</cmdsynopsis>
	</refsynopsisdiv>

	<refsect1>
		<title>Description</title>
		<para>
			<command>process_extractleds</command> extracts LEDs (= bright spots) from a video file in any container or codec FFmpeg can decode. For each video frame, all bright spots are detected and listed in a .spots file (the video file name with its extension replaced by <filename>.spots</filename>, written in the current directory), one line per spot, listing on successive columns the frame number, number of pixels in the spot, x and y coordinates of the spot center, x and y sizes of the spot (defined as standard deviations of the distributions of x and y coordinates of all the pixels in the spot), and spot color (as a YCrCb triplet). With <option>-color</option> or <option>-colors</option>, two columns are appended: hue and color label.
		</para>
	</refsect1>

	<refsect1>
		<title>Options</title>
		<para>
			Options are spelled exactly as listed; any other option prints the usage and exits with status 1.
		</para>
		<variablelist>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>-t</option> <replaceable>threshold</replaceable></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						fixed luminance threshold, 0-255: bright spots consist of pixels brighter than this. By default the threshold is chosen automatically for each frame with Otsu's method.
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>-minsize</option> <replaceable>n</replaceable></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						minimum spot area in pixels (default 1)
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>-maxsize</option> <replaceable>n</replaceable></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						maximum spot area in pixels (default unlimited)
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>-colors</option> <replaceable>N</replaceable></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						number of distinct LED colors to tell apart by hue (default 0, at most 16; e.g. 2 for a red and a green LED); implies <option>-color</option>
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>-color</option></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						append the hue and color-label columns to each line
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>-smooth</option> <replaceable>alpha</replaceable></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						exponential smoothing of spot positions across frames, 0 &lt;= alpha &lt; 1 (default 0 = off; 0.5 moderate, 0.9 heavy)
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>-n</option></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						simulate, i.e. do not write to disk
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>-i</option></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						print the video rate and duration from the file header, then exit
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>-i2</option></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						print the video rate and duration by counting frames, then exit
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>-hide</option></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						accepted and ignored (backward compatibility)
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><replaceable>file</replaceable></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						video file
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
		</variablelist>
	</refsect1>

